    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is drawn, and from where",
      "prov:value": "A diagram of the\ntypes a CONTENT model uses is derived from that model by its own Tool, never\ndrawn: an ArchiMate model's \"Metamodel in use\" page is written by\n`archimate-metamodel` and `archimate-pages` (skill\n[`archimate-models`](../../ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md)). Owner,\n2026-10-31: *\"i dont really like native UML, rather derived\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is drawn, and from where",
      "prov:value": "Register the shape as a family with `derived: true` in the kind's\n`nodeSchemas`, give it a validator node naming its Zod schema, and the\noverview draws it wherever the kind is: the `archimate` kind's\n`archimate-model/v1` (`ArchimateModelSchema`, smart-ra#166 D2). Never invent a\n`$schema` tag on files to get a box drawn.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#166"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is drawn, and from where",
      "prov:value": "**A group is a named sub-graph,** meaning one entry of a harness's declaration\n(`<instance>.json` `directories[]`), drawn as `<instance>/<entry id>`, for\nexample `bootstrap/processes`. The generator never invents a grouping. Owner,\n2026-09-23: *\"sections are sub-graphs in a harness\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the output lives",
      "prov:value": "This is the figure each page shows, in the same\n  `bpmn-figure` markup as the BPMN diagrams, so it gets the same zoom,\n  full-width and export controls (download SVG, download PNG, copy; #1270). An overview with more than three sub-graphs is folded\n  into a near-square grid by hidden links between packages, because ELK\n  otherwise lays unconnected packages in one row.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1270"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the output lives",
      "prov:value": "Each page\n  offers it as a third view, **Interactive**, beside Portrait and Landscape:\n  `assets/js/kg-graph.js` lays it out with the site's vendored Graphviz WASM,\n  and the reader can pan, zoom, find and drag nodes. Owner, 2026-10-09:\n  *\"could use the wasm-graphviz to make the graph visualizers overview more\n  dynamic. also allow users to drag nodes around\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the output lives",
      "prov:value": "So a change to `detangle/results/` makes these pages stale, and\n  `uml:overview` must be re-run with `kg:detangle`. Every page carries `layout: default`: without it the local build\n  rendered the page bare, with no site script and so no zoom controls."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the output lives",
      "prov:value": "It leaves out Bean, the one class read from the `beans` CLI, so\n  unlike the full model it is checked in CI. Owner, 2026-09-23: \"i just want\n  UML (with themes) showing schemas of schema, task, role, user scenario,\n  process, skill, task, test\", plus Actor.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Portrait, landscape and interactive views",
      "prov:value": "Every figure is rendered twice, and the page has a **Portrait / Landscape**\nswitch above it: radio buttons and CSS in `uml.css`, no script, with portrait\nas the default. Owner, 2026-09-23: \"can we have portrait and landscape\nviews?\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Portrait, landscape and interactive views",
      "prov:value": "The `' grid:` comment line in the `.puml` names the packages;\n  - a diagram with edges between classes switches to Graphviz, left to\n    right, with straight-segment (polyline) edges, `nodesep 70` and\n    `ranksep 160`. Orthogonal edges were tried first: Graphviz placed their\n    labels away from the lines and ran lines through boxes (owner: \"make\n    wider, its messy\")."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/uml-overview.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Four things that have already gone wrong",
      "prov:value": "## Four things that have already gone wrong"
    }
  ]
}
